From 6a08eef5166cfb68ec3cf6402a08201dcb270447 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shaun Adams <s.adams@f5.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 21:13:11 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] mt-customprovider-and-strict-routing: catalog bare-ID +
 inference reject
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two narrowly-scoped fixes that together close the custom-provider
inference story for the f5xc multi-tenant overlay. Both surfaced
during the qwen3.6-coder / opencode trace earlier in the audit
(see docs/multi-tenant-f5/12-configstore-tenant-audit.md is the
broader gap-list).

Subfix B — Catalog upsert: accept bare model IDs for custom providers
----------------------------------------------------------------------
framework/modelcatalog/models.go::UpsertModelDataForProvider (and the
sibling UpsertUnfilteredModelDataForProvider) calls ParseModelString
on every model.ID returned by the provider's /v1/models discovery
response. Upstream's filter requires the parsed provider to equal the
queried provider — which means model.ID MUST have an "<provider>/"
prefix, OR the provider must already be registered as known AND the
prefix is the provider's own name.

vLLM and OpenAI-compatible custom backends return BARE IDs
(e.g. {"id":"qwen3.6-coder"}). The upstream filter then drops them
all as "wrong provider", so the catalog stays empty for the custom
provider and auto-resolve at /v1/chat/completions returns
  "no providers found for model X in model catalog to auto-resolve"
even though discovery succeeded and the provider is well-configured.

Fix: add an isCustom bool parameter to UpsertModelDataForProvider /
UpsertUnfilteredModelDataForProvider. When isCustom is true AND the
parsed provider is empty (bare ID, OR a "/" but provider not known to
ParseModelString), accept the model.ID as belonging to the queried
provider. All non-f5xc call paths pass isCustom=false → upstream
behaviour unchanged for the bundled providers.

All six call sites in transports/bifrost-http/server/server.go updated
to pass providerInfo.CustomProviderConfig != nil. Governance test
updated for the new arity.

Subfix A — Inference path: strict tenant-header rejection (env-gated)
----------------------------------------------------------------------
Without strict mode, an inference request whose x-f5xc-tenant header
doesn't resolve to a configured tenant falls through to the root
runtime — Manager.Acquire's loader happily returns an empty-but-valid
BifrostConfig for unknown tids (see server/multitenant.go's
newTenantLoader). That fall-through is correct for OSS single-tenant
callflows but lets MT deployments quietly answer requests against
the wrong runtime when callers mis-type or forget the header.

New env var BIFROST_STRICT_TENANT_ROUTING (default false → no
behavioural change). When set, a new middleware mounted in the
inference chain BETWEEN TenantResolverMiddleware and
TenantDispatcherMiddleware fast-fails inference requests:

  - header absent           → 401 ("header required")
  - header set but unknown  → 404 ("tenant X not found")
  - validator lookup error  → 503 ("tenant lookup failed")
  - default tenant          → short-circuit, no DB hit, pass through

The middleware lives at handlers/tenant_strict_routing.go and is
mounted only on the inference chain (server.go::RegisterInferenceRoutes
~line 1145). The admin chain is intentionally not gated so the
platform tenants surface still works for first-tenant bootstrap.

Tests
-----
- framework/modelcatalog/models_custom_provider_test.go — locks the
  bare-ID truth table for both isCustom=true and =false paths, plus
  an end-to-end test that asserts GetProvidersForModel("qwen3.6-coder")
  returns ["qwen"] after upserting bare IDs (proves auto-resolve
  works for custom providers).
- transports/bifrost-http/handlers/tenant_strict_routing_test.go —
  covers the 4-quadrant truth table (strict on/off × header
  present/absent/known/unknown/default), the validator-error 503
  path, and the strict-without-validator panic guard.

Both test files pass under `go test -race`.

Bugs we DELIBERATELY did NOT fix in this patch
----------------------------------------------
Bug 1 from the earlier audit ("discovery doesn't fire after key add")
turned out to be a false positive — the re-trigger via
handlers.ProviderHandler.attemptModelDiscovery already happens on
createProviderKey / updateProviderKey / deleteProviderKey /
updateProvider in upstream. The "no keys configured" warnings we
chased were just the FIRST-attempt log at provider creation time;
the subsequent key POST re-fires discovery, which then failed only
because of the bad URL in the seeder's qwen base_url (fixed
separately on the go-bifrost-ai seeder repo).

Depends on patches 1, 2, 3, 4, 7 (multitenant package + tenant_id
columns + resolver middleware + dispatcher middleware + runtime
isolation).

Ref: https://jira.f5net.com/browse/XC-25496
